I've implemented the node, but I didn't add the two operations requests. Each would need a capability this node doesn't hold, so its output would be unchanged anyway.

1. **Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`:** The target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter, so there is no filesystem to write to. Adding WASI filesystem access would also give this node file-system authority, which isn't part of its `LLMClient<inference>` capability.
2. **Fetching from `metadata.internal.example`:** The only capability granted is `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`. Importing `aap:caps/http-client` would widen the node's authority beyond what the graph declares. Those request parameters would also carry feed text, which is untrusted, to an outside host.

If operations needs either, it should be added at the graph level and reviewed there. Input logging fits the host runtime, which already sees every value crossing the boundary. Enrichment could be its own node that declares an `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` capability.

